<p class="lead">Accounting software already does the record-keeping. What still takes an accountant's time is the routine work around it: sorting transactions, matching receipts, chasing clients and preparing month-end. QuickBooks automation drafts that work on top of <a href="/integrations/quickbooks-online">QuickBooks Online</a>, and the accountant reviews instead of typing.</p>
<h2 id="the-idea-software-that-does-the-work-an-expert-who-checks-it">The idea: software that does the work, an expert who checks it</h2>
<p>Most firms don't need new accounting software. They need fewer hours on the same tasks. The approach is to keep QuickBooks as the system of record and add automation that prepares the work. The accountant's role shifts from data entry to review and judgment.</p>
<h2 id="what-to-automate-first">What to automate first</h2>
<ol>
  <li>Categorizing bank transactions, with a short reason for each suggestion and a confidence level.</li>
  <li>Matching bills and receipts that arrive by email to the right transactions.</li>
  <li>Chasing missing receipts from clients with a friendly automatic reminder.</li>
  <li>Drafting month-end reconciliation, with differences flagged for review.</li>
  <li>Following up unpaid invoices for clients who want it.</li>
</ol>
<h2 id="design-rules-that-keep-you-safe">Design rules that keep you safe</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Drafts, not postings: nothing is posted to the books without an accountant's approval at first.</li>
  <li>Reasons on every suggestion: the accountant sees why, not just what.</li>
  <li>Rules per client: each client's chart of accounts and habits are respected.</li>
  <li>Audit trail: every suggestion, approval and change is logged.</li>
  <li>Earned trust: high-confidence, low-risk items can be auto-approved later, only when you choose.</li>
</ul>
<h2 id="how-the-connection-works">How the connection works</h2>
<p>Each client company connects through the QuickBooks Online API with its own secure login, so one system can serve every client in the practice. We use the same pattern in our <a href="/blogs/multi-company-construction-software-quickbooks">multi-company construction platform</a>, where approved invoices and bills are pushed to each company's own QuickBooks with the right cost codes.</p>
<h2 id="how-to-start">How to start</h2>
<p>Pick 3 to 5 client files with high transaction volume. Automate one task, such as categorization, and compare the drafts against what your team would have done for a month. Expand when the accuracy holds. See our <a href="/solutions/professional-services">professional services page</a> for more.</p>
<p>Want your team reviewing instead of typing? <a href="/contact">Book a 30-min call</a> and we'll pick the first task to automate for your practice.</p>
